      "title": "GPS L1 C/A navigation message data",
      "institution": "GFZ German Research Centre for Geosciences",
      "comment": "The navigation data >navbits< are stored in units of subframes. Each subframe consists of 10 GPS words, each GPS word contains 30 bits. A subframe is stored as 10 long (32 bit) integers, where GPS bits 1,2,...,30 correspond to bit position 29,28,...,0. Bit position 30 and 31 are not used and initialized to zero. The variable >multiplicity< indicates the number of stations, which recorded this subframe. The variable >time< marks the time corresponding to the start of the subframe. Only validated subframes are included in the data set; therefore, the number of subframes (length of variable >time<) may be less than the maximum value of 86400 s / 6 s = 14400.  Variable >day_of_year<: 1. January = day of year 1.  The data is registered under doi:10.1594/GFZ.ISDC.GNSS/GNSS-GPS-1-NAVBIT  Reference: G. Beyerle, M. Ramatschi, R. Galas, T. Schmidt, J. Wickert, and M. Rothacher, A data archive of GPS navigation messages, GPS Solutions, 13 (1), 35-41, 2009.doi:10.1007/s10291-008-0095-y Erratum: GPS Solutions, 14 (3), 301, 2010. doi:10.1007/s10291-009-0154-z"
